  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual material labeling Trump as a bully",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'he is proving that grown adults can be a bully' because the meme invites the viewer to adopt the judgmental stance expressed in the text, essentially saying 'you are seeing this and agreeing that he is a bully.' The text acts as a direct address to the user's interpretation of the visual material, making the user an active participant in the moral judgment being made. There are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me' in the text, but the framing of the text as a declarative statement that 'he is proving...' implies a shared understanding or agreement from the viewer, projecting the user onto the interpretive act of labeling Trump as a bully.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
